[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2708630130","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103833#issuecomment-2708630130","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103833","id":2708630130,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6hcmpy","user":{"login":"Grublady","id":29121925,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5MTIxOTI1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29121925?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady","html_url":"https://github.com/Grublady","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-09T02:28:42Z","updated_at":"2025-03-09T02:28:42Z","body":"I'm a bit concerned about adding on to the (already quite long) list of `Time` methods that do very similar things.\r\n\r\nAdding a `get_local_datetime_string_from_unix_time` method, which corresponds closely to the current `get_datetime_string_from_unix_time`, also begs the addition of other methods to keep the current parity. For example:\r\n\r\n- `get_date_string_from_unix_time` would want `get_local_date_string_from_unix_time`\r\n- `get_time_string_from_unix_time` would want `get_local_time_string_from_unix_time`\r\n- and so on with each of the `get_..._dict_from_unix_time` methods.\r\n\r\nAnd, adding any more dimensions of complexity in the future would further multiply the number of methods.\r\n\r\nPerhaps the existing methods could have a `local_time` boolean parameter added instead?\r\n\r\nOr, perhaps the `Time` methods could use a broader cleanup anyways—\r\nMaybe a data type representing a moment in time (similar to Swift's `Date`) could work as an intermediary between the different representations (string, dict, Unix) so that we don't have to individually handle every permutation of `get`/`from`.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2708630130/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2708643939","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103833#issuecomment-2708643939","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103833","id":2708643939,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6hcqBj","user":{"login":"aaronfranke","id":1646875,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NDY4NzU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1646875?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke","html_url":"https://github.com/aaronfranke","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-09T03:07:43Z","updated_at":"2025-03-09T03:31:21Z","body":"When I designed the `Time` class, I intentionally kept it simple. It generally does not handle timezone conversions, it only handles the grunt work of converting whatever time you give it between formats. As @Grublady points out, a lot of these methods would need local versions. However, a local version itself is potentially not enough, people could ask for versions of the functions that involve working with any timezone, which would quickly explode into so many combinations.\r\n\r\nAlso, which part is local? This function expects a non-local input and gives a local output, but what about a function that goes the other way? (if both are local, or both are non-local, the current functions work fine). In this use case it's obvious, but how can you effectively communicate the local-ness to readers in all future use-cases and all functions?\r\n\r\nThis is why I don't think a new method should be added here. The call sites needing a local time can call `OS::get_singleton()->get_time_zone_info()`, add the offset, and then call the `Time` method.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2708643939/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2709036504","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103833#issuecomment-2709036504","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103833","id":2709036504,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6heJ3Y","user":{"login":"nobbele","id":17962514,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3OTYyNTE0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17962514?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nobbele","html_url":"https://github.com/nobbele","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nobbele/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nobbele/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nobbele/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nobbele/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nobbele/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nobbele/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nobbele/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nobbele/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nobbele/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-09T19:41:43Z","updated_at":"2025-03-09T19:42:10Z","body":"Yeah I had the same concerns here. I'll change it to just add the timezone bias for this component.\r\n\r\n-----------------------\r\n\r\n>Perhaps the existing methods could have a local_time boolean parameter added instead?\r\n\r\nI thought of that but considering it already has a `use_space` parameter, I thought it would be kinda ugly to have 2 optional parameters.\r\n\r\n>Maybe a data type representing a moment in time\r\n\r\nI think so too, but it'd definitely be another discussion/PR.\r\n\r\n>Also, which part is local\r\n\r\nDoes \"unix time\" not implicitly mean UTC+0?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2709036504/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2709041943","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103833#issuecomment-2709041943","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103833","id":2709041943,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6heLMX","user":{"login":"nobbele","id":17962514,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3OTYyNTE0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17962514?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nobbele","html_url":"https://github.com/nobbele","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nobbele/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nobbele/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nobbele/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nobbele/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nobbele/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nobbele/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nobbele/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nobbele/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nobbele/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-09T19:57:05Z","updated_at":"2025-03-09T19:57:05Z","body":"I updated it by adding `get_last_edited_string()` to `ProjectList::Item` ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2709041943/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2715353041","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103833#issuecomment-2715353041","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103833","id":2715353041,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6h2P_R","user":{"login":"aaronfranke","id":1646875,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NDY4NzU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1646875?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke","html_url":"https://github.com/aaronfranke","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-11T18:32:22Z","updated_at":"2025-03-11T18:32:22Z","body":"Note that, in the case of DST, this will show the \"incorrect\" time. If a project is edited before the DST change, then the last edited time will show as \"one hour off\" after the DST change, and likewise for the other change. However, handling complex conversions like these is probably out-of-scope for Godot, so we could just not handle this. ¯\\\\\\_(ツ)_/¯","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2715353041/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2715371936","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103833#issuecomment-2715371936","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103833","id":2715371936,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6h2Umg","user":{"login":"nobbele","id":17962514,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3OTYyNTE0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17962514?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nobbele","html_url":"https://github.com/nobbele","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nobbele/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nobbele/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nobbele/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nobbele/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nobbele/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nobbele/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nobbele/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nobbele/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nobbele/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-11T18:39:08Z","updated_at":"2025-03-11T18:39:08Z","body":"> Note that, in the case of DST, this will show the \"incorrect\" time. If a project is edited before the DST change, then the last edited time will show as \"one hour off\" after the DST change, and likewise for the other change. However, handling complex conversions like these is probably out-of-scope for Godot, so we could just not handle this. ¯\\_(ツ)_/¯\r\n\r\nStoring the last edited timezone offset (like the version control system does) could work :sweat_smile: \r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2715371936/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2906722231","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103833#issuecomment-2906722231","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103833","id":2906722231,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6tQQ-3","user":{"login":"nobbele","id":17962514,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3OTYyNTE0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17962514?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nobbele","html_url":"https://github.com/nobbele","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nobbele/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nobbele/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.git